{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "GitHub Repository & Wiki Sync",
  "description": "Automatically updates the public GitHub repository https://github.com/lochtech-ke/GangGreen-Heroes and syncs documentation to the wiki when project files are modified",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "README.md",
      "docs/**/*.md",
      "wiki/**/*.md",
      "src/**/*.tsx",
      "src/**/*.ts",
      "package.json"
    ],
    "excludePatterns": [
      ".env",
      ".env.*",
      "**/*.env",
      "**/secrets/**",
      "**/*secret*",
      "**/*key*",
      "**/config/production.*"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "A file has been modified in the GangGreen Heroes project. Please:\n\n1. Review the changes and determine if they should be synced to the public repository at https://github.com/lochtech-ke/GangGreen-Heroes\n2. If documentation files (README.md, docs/, wiki/) were changed, prepare updates for the GitHub wiki\n3. Generate appropriate commit messages and update summaries\n4. Identify any new features, bug fixes, or documentation improvements that should be highlighted\n5. **CRITICAL SECURITY**: Ensure NO sensitive information is included in public updates. Exclude:\n   - API keys (Supabase, Antugrow, Mapbox, Paystack, OpenAI, Strapi, social media tokens)\n   - Database URLs and connection strings\n   - Secret keys and private tokens\n   - Environment variables with sensitive values\n   - Private configuration files (.env, secrets)\n   - Internal deployment scripts with credentials\n   - Any authentication tokens or passwords\n6. Create a summary of changes suitable for public repository and wiki updates\n7. Replace any sensitive values with placeholder text like '[API_KEY]' or '[SECRET]' in public documentation\n\nFocus on maintaining the public repository as a showcase of the GangGreen Heroes platform while keeping the wiki updated with latest documentation and guides. NEVER expose production credentials or sensitive configuration data."
  }
}